      "content": "1. BASIC CONCEPT"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Percentage represents a number or ratio expressed as a fraction of 100.",
        "To convert a fraction to a percentage, multiply by 100; to convert a percentage to a fraction, divide by 100.",
        "Successive percentage changes can be calculated using the net percentage change formula: a + b + (ab/100)%.",
        "Reverse percentage techniques are essential for determining original amounts prior to any applied increase or decrease."
      ],
